          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xìngqù is built from xìng and qù, both inherited from Middle Chinese, xingH and tshjuH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary glosses the second 'to tend towards'; it gives no sense for the first in this tone, and its level-tone reading means 'to rise'. How the pair came to mean an interest is not settled."
